>> title: Eggs Benedict
>> category: Eggs
>> tags: eggs, hollandaise, breakfast, poached, brunch
>> counters: Diner
>> aka: benedict, eggs benny, eggs benedictine, poached eggs benedict
>> pairs-with: hollandaise, english-muffins
>> servings: 2
>> time: 20 min
>> slack: unforgiving — the hollandaise breaks if it is held hot or reheated, so it and the eggs are both made to be eaten straight away

>> step: crisp both faces 2 min
Crisp @Canadian bacon{4%slices}(1/4-in thick) in @unsalted butter{1%tsp}(5 g) in a #skillet{} over medium heat ~fry{2%min}, until the edges brown and cup slightly.

>> step: toast the split muffins 2 min
Toast @english muffins{2}(split with a fork, never a knife) cut side up under a #broiler{} ~toast{2%min}, until the torn peaks colour.

>> step: poach 3 min in barely moving water
Poach @eggs{4%large} in @water{2%qt}(1.9 L) with @distilled white vinegar{1%Tbs}(15 mL) ~poach{3%min}, in water held just below a shiver — a boil beats the whites into rags.

>> step: stack, sauce, and eat it standing up
Stack @&(~2)crisped bacon{} on @&(~3)toasted muffins{}, lift @&(~1)poached eggs{} out with a slotted spoon and blot them on a towel, then flood the lot with @hollandaise{1%cup}(240 mL) and finish with @chives{1%Tbs}(sliced) and @cayenne{1%pinch}.
